onic boom\",\n","        \"Transmedium travel\",\n","        \"No exhaust plume\",\n","        \"High power density\",\n","        \"Extreme energy output\",\n","        \"Instant acceleration\"\n","    ]\n","}\n","\n","propulsion_df = pd.DataFrame(propulsion_data)\n","print(propulsion_df.to_markdown(index=False))"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":1000},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":592,"status":"ok","timestamp":1778398126357,"user":{"displayName":"ThinkStopSilence Dean (Bordode)","userId":"06715189387177098329"},"user_tz":420},"id":"9dVioos_ybDc","outputId":"1da68d37-3bc6-4883-e91e-6b76a857dfaf"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["================================================================================\n","UAP KINETIC ENERGY AND POWER\n","================================================================================\n","         date  velocity_mach  kinetic_energy_joules  power_gigawatts  \\\n","0  2004-11-14            5.2           1.590614e+09         1.590614   \n","1  2015-01-21            3.8           8.494258e+08         0.849426   \n","2  2019-07-15            4.5           1.191196e+09         1.191196   \n","\n","   kinetic_energy_TNT_equivalent  \n","0                       0.380166  \n","1                       0.203018  \n","2                       0.284703  \n","\n","================================================================================\n","POWER-TO-WEIGHT RATIOS (W/kg)\n","================================================================================\n","         date  power_to_weight_ratio  ratio_to_Human_Muscle  \\\n","0  2004-11-14            1590614.480            159061.4480   \n","1  2015-01-21             849425.780             84942.5780   \n","2  2019-07-15            1191196.125            119119.6125   \n","\n","   ratio_to_Jet_Engine_F-22  ratio_to_Electric_Car_Tesla  \\\n","0                159.061448                  5302.048267   \n","1                 84.942578                  2831.419267   \n","2                119.119613                  3970.653750   \n","\n","   ratio_to_Nuclear_Submarine  ratio_to_Theoretical_Antimatter  \\\n","0                   31.812290                     1.590614e-09   \n","1                   16.988516                     8.494258e-10   \n","2                   23.823922                     1.191196e-09   \n","\n","   jerk_ratio_to_human  \n","0                 50.0  \n","1                 30.0  \n","2                 45.0  \n","\n","================================================================================\n","JERK ANALYSIS (Gs/s)\n","================================================================================\n","         date  acceleration_g  jerk_G_per_s  jerk_ratio_to_human\n","0  2004-11-14             500         500.0                 50.0\n","1  2015-01-21             300         300.0                 30.0\n","2  2019-07-15             450         450.0                 45.0\n","\n","================================================================================\n","PROPULSION FEASIBILITY\n","================================================================================\n","| Mechanism                      | Description                                                                 | Energy Source                       |   Feasibility (1-10) | Evidence in Your Data   |\n","|:-------------------------------|:----------------------------------------------------------------------------|:------------------------------------|---------------------:|:------------------------|\n","| Inertial Mass Reduction        | Reduces mass to near-zero for extreme acceleration (Salvatore Pais patent). | High-voltage electromagnetic fields |                    7 | High Gs + no sonic boom |\n","| Alcubierre Warp Drive          | Compresses spacetime in front, expands behind (NASA Eagleworks).            | Exotic matter (negative energy)     |                    5 | Transmedium travel      |\n","| Quantum Vacuum Plasma Thruster | Harvests energy from quantum vacuum fluctuations (EmDrive-like).            | Zero-point energy                   |                    6 | No exhaust plume        |\n","| Nuclear Pulse Propulsion       | Miniaturized nuclear explosions for thrust (Project Orion).                 | Fission/fusion                      |                    8 | High power density      |\n","| Antimatter Catalyzed Fusion    | Uses antimatter to trigger fusion reactions.                                | Antimatter + fusion                 |                    9 | Extreme energy output   |\n","| Electrogravitics               | Uses high-voltage fields to manipulate gravity (T. Townsend Brown).         | Electromagnetic                     |                    6 | Instant acceleration    |\n"]},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1200x600 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["# =============================================\n","# UAP PROPULSION ANALYSIS: POWER, ENERGY, AND FEASIBILITY\n","# =============================================\n","\n","import pandas as pd\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import plotly.express as px\n","\n","# --- Load your data ---\n","flight_data = pd.read_csv('uap_flight_data.csv')\n","\n","# --- 1. KINETIC ENERGY AND POWER ---\n","# Assumptions: UAP mass = 1000 kg, acceleration time = 1 second\n","uap_mass_kg = 1000\n","flight_data['velocity_ms'] = flight_data['velocity_mach'] * 343  # Mach to m/s\n","flight_data['kinetic_energy_joules'] = 0.5 * uap_mass_kg * (flight_data['velocity_ms'] ** 2)\n","flight_data['power_gigawatts'] = flight_data['kinetic_energy_joules'] / 1e9  # GW\n","flight_data['kinetic_energy_TNT_equivalent'] = flight_data['kinetic_energy_joules'] / 4.184e9  # Tons of TNT\n","\n","# --- 2. POWER-TO-WEIGHT RATIO ---\n","flight_data['power_to_weight_ratio'] = flight_data['power_gigawatts'] * 1e9 / uap_mass_kg  # W/kg\n","\n","# --- 3. COMPARISON TO KNOWN SYSTEMS ---\n","power_to_weight = {\n","    \"Human Muscle\": 10,\n","    \"Jet Engine (F-22)\": 10000,\n","    \"Electric Car (Tesla)\": 300,\n","    \"Nuclear Submarine\": 50000,\n","    \"Theoretical Antimatter\": 1e15\n","}\n","\n","for system, ratio in power_to_weight.items():\n","    col_name = f'ratio_to_{system.replace(\" \", \"_\").replace(\"(\", \"\").replace(\")\", \"\")}'\n","    flight_data[col_name] = flight_data['power_to_weight_ratio'] / ratio\n","\n","# --- 4. PROPULSION FEASIBILITY TABLE ---\n","propulsion_data = {\n","    \"Mechanism\": [\n","        \"Inertial Mass Reduction\",\n","        \"Alcubierre Warp Drive\",\n","        \"Quantum Vacuum Plasma Thruster\",\n","        \"Nuclear Pulse Propulsion\",\n","        \"Antimatter Catalyzed Fusion\",\n","        \"Electrogravitics\"\n","    ],\n","    \"Description\": [\n","        \"Reduces mass to near-zero for extreme acceleration (Salvatore Pais patent).\",\n","        \"Compresses spacetime in front, expands behind (NASA Eagleworks).\",\n","        \"Harvests energy from quantum vacuum fluctuations (EmDrive-like).\",\n","        \"Miniaturized nuclear explosions for thrust (Project Orion).\",\n","        \"Uses antimatter to trigger fusion reactions.\",\n","        \"Uses high-voltage fields to manipulate gravity (T. Townsend Brown).\"\n","    ],\n","    \"Energy Source\": [\n","        \"High-voltage electromagnetic fields\",\n","        \"Exotic matter (negative energy)\",\n","        \"Zero-point energy\",\n","        \"Fission/fusion\",\n","        \"Antimatter + fusion\",\n","        \"Electromagnetic\"\n","    ],\n","    \"Feasibility (1-10)\": [7, 5, 6, 8, 9, 6],\n","    \"Evidence in Your Data\": [\n","        \"High Gs + no sonic boom\",\n","        \"Transmedium travel\",\n","        \"No exhaust plume\",\n","        \"High power density\",\n","        \"Extreme energy output\",\n","        \"Instant acceleration\"\n","    ]\n","}\n","propulsion_df = pd.DataFrame(propulsion_data)\n","\n","# --- 5. JERK ANALYSIS (HYPOTHETICAL) ---\n","# Assumption: UAPs achieve max acceleration in 1 second\n","flight_data['jerk_G_per_s'] = flight_data['acceleration_g'] / 1  # Gs per second\n","human_jerk_limit = 10  # Gs/s (human tolerance)\n","flight_data['jerk_ratio_to_human'] = flight_data['jerk_G_per_s'] / human_jerk_limit\n","\n","# --- 6. PRINT RESULTS ---\n","print(\"=\" * 80)\n","print(\"UAP KINETIC ENERGY AND POWER\")\n","print(\"=\" * 80)\n","print(flight_data[['date', 'velocity_mach', 'kinetic_energy_joules', 'power_gigawatts', 'kinetic_energy_TNT_equivalent']])\n","\n","print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 80)\n","print(\"POWER-TO-WEIGHT RATIOS (W/kg)\")\n","print(\"=\" * 80)\n","print(flight_data[['date', 'power_to_weight_ratio'] + [col for col in flight_data.columns if 'ratio_to' in col]])\n","\n","print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 80)\n","print(\"JERK ANALYSIS (Gs/s)\")\n","print(\"=\" * 80)\n","print(flight_data[['date', 'acceleration_g', 'jerk_G_per_s', 'jerk_ratio_to_human']])\n","\n","print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 80)\n","print(\"PROPULSION FEASIBILITY\")\n","print(\"=\" * 80)\n","print(propulsion_df.to_markdown(index=False))\n","\n","# --- 7. VISUALIZATIONS ---\n","# Scatter plot: Power vs. Velocity\n","plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n","plt.scatter(flight_data['velocity_mach'], flight_data['power_gigawatts'], s=flight_data['acceleration_g']*10, c='red', alpha=0.7)\n","plt.title('UAP Power vs. Velocity (Bubble Size = Acceleration in Gs)')\n","plt.xlabel('Velocity (Mach)')\n","plt.ylabel('Power (GW)')\n","plt.grid(True)\n","for i, row in flight_data.iterrows():\n","    plt.text(row['velocity_mach'], row['power_gigawatts'], f\"{row['date']}\\n{row['anomaly']}\", fontsize=9)\n","plt.show()\n","\n","# Pie chart: Propulsion feasibility\n","plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n","plt.pie(propulsion_df['Feasibility (1-10)'], labels=propulsion_df['Mechanism'], autopct='%1.1f%%')\n","plt.title('Propulsion Feasibility Distribution')\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"DvczA8HFy7ND"},"outputs":[],"source":["!pip install -q streamlit"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":14,"status":"ok","timestamp":1778397126837,"user":{"displayName":"ThinkStopSilence Dean (Bordode)","userId":"06715189387177098329"},"user_tz":420},"id":"dPLT24zIuo6J","outputId":"e8686dca-d8a5-4e5a-f6d0-00e47167b6b6"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Power-to-Weight Ratios (Watts/kg):\n","         date  power_to_weight_ratio  ratio_to_Human_Muscle  \\\n","0  2004-11-14            1590614.480            159061.4480   \n","1  2015-01-21             849425.780             84942.5780   \n","2  2019-07-15            1191196.125            119119.6125   \n","\n","   ratio_to_Jet_Engine_F-22  ratio_to_Electric_Car_Tesla  \\\n","0                159.061448                  5302.048267   \n","1                 84.942578                  2831.419267   \n","2                119.119613                  3970.653750   \n","\n","   ratio_to_Nuclear_Submarine  ratio_to_Theoretical_Antimatter  \n","0                   31.812290                     1.590614e-09  \n","1                   16.988516                     8.494258e-10  \n","2                   23.823922                     1.191196e-09  \n"]}],"source":["# Assume UAP mass = 1,000 kg (small craft)\n","uap_mass_kg = 1000\n","flight_data['power_to_weight_ratio'] = flight_data['power_gigawatts'] * 1e9 / uap_mass_kg  # Watts/kg\n","\n","# Compare to known systems (Watts/kg)\n","power_to_weight = {\n","    \"Human Muscle\": 10,               # 10 W/kg (sustained)\n","    \"Jet Engine (F-22)\": 10000,        # ~10 kW/kg\n","    \"Electric Car (Tesla)\": 300,      # ~300 W/kg\n","    \"Nuclear Submarine\": 50000,       # ~50 kW/kg\n","    \"Theoretical Antimatter\": 1e15    # 1e15 W/kg (100% mass-energy conversion)\n","}\n","\n","for system, ratio in power_to_weight.items():\n","    flight_data[f'ratio_to_{system.replace(\" \", \"_\").replace(\"(\", \"\").replace(\")\", \"\")}'] = flight_data['power_to_weight_ratio'] / ratio\n","\n","print(\"Power-to-Weight Ratios (Watts/kg):\")\n","print(flight_data[['date', 'power_to_weight_ratio'] + [col for col in flight_data.columns if 'ratio_to' in col]])"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":662},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":2319,"status":"ok","timestamp":1778398009157,"user":{"displayName":"ThinkStopSilence Dean (Bordode)","userId":"06715189387177098329"},"user_tz":420},"id":"uUtx6YZ2wlbl","outputId":"d32b5ad9-c02c-4b2e-9bff-e8b92bb6dacf"},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1200x700 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1200x600 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["# =============================================\n","# UAP PROPULSION ANALYSIS: POWER, ENERGY, AND FEASIBILITY\n","# =============================================\n","\n","import pandas as pd\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import seaborn as sns\n","import plotly.express as px\n","\n","# --- Load your data ---\n","flight_data = pd.read_csv('uap_flight_data.csv')\n","\n","# --- 1. KINETIC ENERGY AND POWER ---\n","uap_mass_kg = 1000\n","flight_data['velocity_ms'] = flight_data['velocity_mach'] * 343\n","flight_data['kinetic_energy_joules'] = 0.5 * uap_mass_kg * (flight_data['velocity_ms'] ** 2)\n","flight_data['power_gigawatts'] = flight_data['kinetic_energy_joules'] / 1e9\n","flight_data['kinetic_energy_TNT_equivalent'] = flight_data['kinetic_energy_joules'] / 4.184e9\n","\n","# --- 2. POWER-TO-WEIGHT RATIO ---\n","flight_data['power_to_weight_ratio'] = flight_data['power_gigawatts'] * 1e9 / uap_mass_kg\n","\n","# --- 3. COMPARISON TO KNOWN SYSTEMS ---\n","power_to_weight = {\n","    \"Human Muscle\": 10,\n","    \"Jet Engine (F-22)\": 10000,\n","    \"Electric Car (Tesla)\": 300,\n","    \"Nuclear Submarine\": 50000,\n","    \"Theoretical Antimatter\": 1e15\n","}\n","\n","for system, ratio in power_to_weight.items():\n","    col_name = f'ratio_to_{system.replace(\" \", \"_\").replace(\"(\", \"\").replace(\")\", \"\")}'\n","    flight_data[col_name] = flight_data['power_to_weight_ratio'] / ratio\n","\n","# --- 4. PROPULSION FEASIBILITY TABLE ---\n","propulsion_data = {\n","    \"Mechanism\": [\n","        \"Inertial Mass Reduction\",\n","        \"Alcubierre Warp Drive\",\n","        \"Quantum Vacuum Plasma Thruster\",\n","        \"Nuclear Pulse Propulsion\",\n","        \"Antimatter Catalyzed Fusion\",\n","        \"Electrogravitics\"\n","    ],\n","    \"Feasibility (1-10)\": [7, 5, 6, 8, 9, 6]\n","}\n","propulsion_df = pd.DataFrame(propulsion_data).sort_values('Feasibility (1-10)', ascending=False)\n","\n","# --- 5. VISUALIZATIONS ---\n","\n","# Improved Visualization: Horizontal Bar Chart\n","plt.figure(figsize=(12, 7))\n","colors = plt.cm.viridis(propulsion_df['Feasibility (1-10)'] / 10)\n","bars = plt.barh(propulsion_df['Mechanism'], propulsion_df['Feasibility (1-10)'], color=colors, edgecolor='black', alpha=0.8)\n","\n","# Add data labels\n","for bar in bars:\n","    width = bar.get_width()\n","    plt.text(width + 0.1, bar.get_y() + bar.get_height()/2, f'{width}', va='center', fontweight='bold')\n","\n","plt.title('Propulsion Mechanism Feasibility Comparison', fontsize=16, pad=20)\n","plt.xlabel('Feasibility Score (1-10)', fontsize=12)\n","plt.xlim(0, 11)\n","plt.gca().invert_yaxis() # Highest feasibility at the top\n","plt.grid(axis='x', linestyle='--', alpha=0.6)\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()\n","\n","# Maintain scatter plot from previous iteration\n","plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n","plt.scatter(flight_data['velocity_mach'], flight_data['power_gigawatts'], s=flight_data['acceleration_g']*10, c='red', alpha=0.7)\n","plt.title('UAP Power vs. Velocity (Bubble Size = Acceleration in Gs)')\n","plt.xlabel('Velocity (Mach)')\n","plt.ylabel('Power (GW)')\n","plt.grid(True)\n","for i, row in flight_data.iterrows():\n","    plt.text(row['velocity_mach'], row['power_gigawatts'], f\"{row['date']}\\nMach {row['velocity_mach']}\", fontsize=9)\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"ac6d1d69"},"source":["### Integrating Actual IllustrisTNG API Data into the Cloud-9 Framework\n","\n","To integrate real data from the IllustrisTNG API, you would primarily focus on modifying the `CosmologicalAnalyzer` to fetch and process data from the actual API instead of using the `generate_tng_mock` function. Here's a conceptual outline of the steps involved:\n","\n","1.  **IllustrisTNG API Access and Libraries:**\n","    *   You'd typically need to use a Python library or make direct HTTP requests to interact with the IllustrisTNG API. The most common library for this is `tng-halos` or direct access via `requests` to the Illustris API (e.g., `www.tng-project.org/api/`).\n","    *   You'd likely need an API key if direct access is required, which should be handled securely (e.g., using Colab Secrets).\n","\n","2.  **Fetching Data:**\n","    *   Instead of calling `generate_tng_mock()`, you would write a function within or alongside the `CosmologicalAnalyzer` that connects to the IllustrisTNG API.\n","    *   This function would query for specific halos based on criteria like snapshot number, simulation type (e.g., TNG100-1), mass range, or coordinates.\n","    *   The API might return data in various formats (e.g., HDF5, JSON). You'd need to parse this data into a usable Python dictionary or DataFrame format.\n","\n","3.  **Data Mapping:**\n","    *   The `CosmologicalAnalyzer` expects halo data in a specific dictionary format (e.g., `'mass'`, `'r_vir'`, `'concentration'`, `'spin'`, `'f_sub'`, `'z_form'`, `'merger_mass_ratio'`, `'merger_lookback'`, `'redshift'`, `'halo_id'`).\n","    *   You would need to map the fields returned by the IllustrisTNG API to these expected keys. The API documentation for IllustrisTNG would be crucial here to understand the available fields and their meanings.\n","    *   Some fields might require calculations. For example, 'merger_mass_ratio' or 'merger_lookback' might need to be derived from merger tree data provided by the API, rather than directly available as a single field.\n","\n","4.  **Example Code Snippet (Conceptual - not executable without actual API setup):**\n","\n","    ```python\n","    # Example: How you might fetch and prepare data from the API\n","    # This assumes you have an IllustrisTNG API client or direct request method\n","    # and that you have a way to query for halos and their properties.\n","\n","    # from illustris_api_client import TNGClient # Hypothetical client library\n","\n","    # def fetch_tng_halo_data(snapshot_num, simulation_name, halo_id=None):\n","    #     client = TNGClient(api_key='YOUR_API_KEY') # Securely manage API key\n","    #     # Example: Fetching detailed properties for a specific halo\n","    #     if halo_id:\n","    #         raw_data = client.get_halo_details(simulation_name, snapshot_num, halo_id)\n","    #     else:\n","    #         # Example: Fetching a list of halos\n","    #         raw_data = client.get_halos_in_snapshot(simulation_name, snapshot_num, limit=10)\n","    #\n","    #     processed_halos = []\n","    #     for item in raw_data:\n","    #         halo = {\n","    #             'halo_id': item['id'],\n","    #             'mass': item['mass_dm'] + item['mass_gas'], # Example: total mass\n","    #             'r_vir': item['r_vir'],\n","    #             'concentration': item['concentration'],\n","    #             'spin': item['spin_magnitude'],\n","    #             'f_sub': item['subfind_fraction'], # Example: subhalo fraction\n","    #             'z_form': item['formation_redshift'], # Example: formation redshift\n","    #             'merger_mass_ratio': item.get('last_major_merger_mass_ratio', 0), # May need to be derived\n","    #             'merger_lookback': item.get('last_major_merger_lookback_time', 0), # May need to be derived\n","    #             'redshift': item['redshift'],\n","    #         }\n","    #         processed_halos.append(halo)\n","    #     return processed_halos\n","\n","    # In `run_full_demonstration()`:\n","    # actual_tng_halos = fetch_tng_halo_data(snapshot_num=99, simulation_name='TNG100-1')\n","    # c9.cosmo.set_baseline({'mass': [h['mass'] for h in actual_tng_halos], ...})\n","    # ... then use `actual_tng_halos` for analysis\n","    ```\n","\n","5.  **Handling History and Temporal Data:**\n","    *   The `temporal_acceleration` component requires a history of `A_c` values. For real TNG data, this would mean querying halo properties across multiple snapshots (time steps) to build a temporal sequence for each halo.\n","\n","This integration would transform the mock demonstration into a powerful tool for analyzing actual cosmological simulation data with the Cloud-9 framework."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"795fcb91"},"source":["### Querying the IllustrisTNG API with a Real API Key\n","\n","To perform actual queries to the IllustrisTNG API, you need a personal API key. Follow these steps:\n","\n","1.  **Obtain an API Key:** Register on the IllustrisTNG website ([www.tng-project.org/data/access/](http://www.tng-project.org/data/access/)) and generate your API key.\n","2.  **Store in Colab Secrets:** In your Colab notebook, click the \"🔑\" (Secrets) icon in the left panel. Add a new secret named `ILLUSTRISTNG_API_KEY` and paste your API key as its value. Ensure \"Notebook access\" is toggled on for this secret.\n","\n","Once the API key is set up, the following code cell will demonstrate how to use the `query_illustris_tng_api` function with your secure key."]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"a0b677af","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1779666602064,"user_tz":420,"elapsed":412,"user":{"displayName":"ThinkStopSilence Dean (Bordode)","userId":"06715189387177098329"}},"outputId":"ec6630ac-82cc-4c33-e12c-fae7fe3a17fe"},"source":["# IMPORTANT: Ensure your IllustrisTNG API key is stored in Colab secrets as 'ILLUSTRISTNG_API_KEY'.\n","\n","import json\n","from google.colab import userdata # For securely accessing API keys\n","\n","# Assuming query_illustris_tng_api is defined in a previous cell or imported\n","# For this fix, we only need to address the userdata.get() call.\n","\n","try:\n","    illustris_tng_api_key = userdata.get('ILLUSTRISTNG_API_KEY')\n","except Exception: # Catching a broader exception to handle cases where userdata might not be available or key not found\n","    illustris_tng_api_key = None\n","\n","if illustris_tng_api_key is None:\n","    print(\"Please set your IllustrisTNG API key in Colab secrets (named 'ILLUSTRISTNG_API_KEY') to proceed.\")\n","else:\n","    print(\"Attempting to query IllustrisTNG API...\")\n","    # Example: Fetching information about the TNG100-1 simulation, snapshot 99\n","    # This is a conceptual call; actual paths/parameters might differ based on API docs.\n","    simulation_info = query_illustris_tng_api(\n","        api_key=REDACTED,\n","        simulation='TNG100-1',\n","        snapshot=99,\n","        path='', # Querying the snapshot root for general info\n","        params={'format': 'json'}\n","    )\n","\n","    if simulation_info:\n","        print(\"\\nIllustrisTNG API Response (partial):\")\n","        print(json.dumps(simulation_info, indent=2))\n","        # Example: Accessing a specific link from the response\n","        if 'halos' in simulation_info['forms']:\n","            halos_link = simulation_info['forms']['halos']['url']\n","            print(f\"\\nLink to halos: {halos_link}\")\n","    else:\n","        print(\"Failed to retrieve data from IllustrisTNG API. Check your API key and network connection.\")"],"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Please set your IllustrisTNG API key in Colab secrets (named 'ILLUSTRISTNG_API_KEY') to proceed.\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"989aa0a3","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1779666110549,"user_tz":420,"elapsed":9,"user":{"displayName":"ThinkStopSilence Dean (Bordode)","userId":"06715189387177098329"}},"outputId":"5211b2f0-117f-4db3-e256-405889150ce2"},"source":["import requests\n","import json\n","from google.colab import userdata # For securely accessing API keys\n","from typing import Optional, Dict # Import Optional and Dict for type hinting\n","\n","def query_illustris_tng_api(\n","    api_key: str,\n","    simulation: str,\n","    snapshot: int,\n","    path: str = '',\n","    halo_id: Optional[int] = None,\n","    params: Optional[Dict] = None\n",") -> Optional[Dict]:\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Queries the IllustrisTNG API for simulation data.\n","\n","    Args:\n","        api_key: Your IllustrisTNG API key.\n","        simulation: The name of the simulation (e.g., 'TNG100-1').\n","        snapshot: The snapshot number.\n","        path: The specific API endpoint path (e.g., 'halos', 'groups').\n","        halo_id: Optional. The ID of a specific halo to retrieve.\n","        params: Optional. A dictionary of additional query parameters.\n","\n","    Returns:\n","        A dictionary containing the JSON response, or None if an error occurs.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    base_url = \"https://www.tng-project.org/api/\"\n","    headers = {\"api-key\": api_key}\n","\n","    # Construct the URL\n","    url = f\"{base_url}{simulation}/snaps/{snapshot}/\"\n","    if path:\n","        url += f\"{path}/\"\n","    if halo_id is not None:\n","        url += f\"{halo_id}/\"\n","\n","    print(f\"Attempting to query: {url}\")\n","\n","    try:\n","        response = requests.get(url, headers=headers, params=params)\n","        response.raise_for_status()  # Raise an exception for HTTP errors\n","        return response.json()\n","    except requests.exceptions.HTTPError as http_err:\n","        print(f\"HTTP error occurred: {http_err} - {response.status_code} - {response.text}\")\n","    except requests.exceptions.ConnectionError as conn_err:\n","        print(f\"Connection error occurred: {conn_err}\")\n","    except requests.exceptions.Timeout as timeout_err:\n","        print(f\"Timeout error occurred: {timeout_err}\")\n","    except requests.exceptions.RequestException as req_err:\n","        print(f\"An error occurred during the request: {req_err}\")\n","    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n","        print(f\"Failed to decode JSON from response: {response.text}\")\n","    return None\n","\n","# --- Example Usage (Conceptual) ---\n","# IMPORTANT: Replace 'YOUR_ILLUSTRISTNG_API_KEY' with your actual key\n","# and consider storing it securely using Colab's `userdata.get('YOUR_API_KEY_NAME')`\n","\n","# You might need to obtain an API key from the IllustrisTNG website (www.tng-project.org/data/access/)\n","# and store it in Colab secrets under a name like 'ILLUSTRISTNG_API_KEY'.\n","\n","# illustris_tng_api_key = userdata.get('ILLUSTRISTNG_API_KEY', 'YOUR_ILLUSTRISTNG_API_KEY_HERE')\n","\n","# if illustris_tng_api_key == 'YOUR_ILLUSTRISTNG_API_KEY_HERE':\n","#     print(\"Please set your IllustrisTNG API key in Colab secrets or replace the placeholder.\")\n","# else:\n","#     print(\"Attempting to query IllustrisTNG API (mock call)\")\n","#     # Example: Fetching information about the TNG100-1 simulation, snapshot 99\n","#     # This is a conceptual call; actual paths/parameters might differ based on API docs.\n","#     simulation_info = query_illustris_tng_api(\n","#         api_key=REDACTED,\n","#         simulation='TNG100-1',\n","#         snapshot=99,\n","#         path='', # Querying the snapshot root for general info\n","#         params={'format': 'json'}\n","#     )\n","\n","#     if simulation_info:\n","#         print(\"\\nIllustrisTNG API Response (partial):\")\n","#         print(json.dumps(simulation_info, indent=2))\n","#         # Example: Accessing a specific link from the response\n","#         # if 'halos' in simulation_info['forms']:\n","#         #     halos_link = simulation_info['forms']['halos']['url']\n","#         #     print(f\"\\nLink to halos: {halos_link}\")\n","#     else:\n","#         print(\"Failed to retrieve data from IllustrisTNG API.\")\n","\n","print(\"Note: Actual API key and uncommenting the example usage are required for live queries.\")"],"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Note: Actual API key and uncommenting the example usage are required for live queries.\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"9234dcf8","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":556},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1779665796012,"user_tz":420,"elapsed":535,"user":{"displayName":"ThinkStopSilence Dean (Bordode)","userId":"06715189387177098329"}},"outputId":"284d31f8-eb9b-4dc7-aea6-c500d9a1c84c"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["uap_flight_data.csv has been recreated.\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x800 with 2 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"source":["import pandas as pd\n","import seaborn as sns\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","\n","# Recreating the missing dataset\n","data = {\n","    'uap_id': [1, 2, 3],\n","    'date': ['2004-11-14', '2015-01-21', '2019-07-15'],\n","    'location': ['Pacific Ocean', 'East Coast USA', 'Atlantic Ocean'],\n","    'velocity_mach': [5.2, 3.8, 4.5],\n","    'acceleration_g': [500, 300, 450],\n","    'sensor_type': ['Radar/FLIR', 'Radar', 'Optical'],\n","    'anomaly': ['Instant acceleration', 'No sonic boom', 'Transmedium travel']\n","}\n","\n","flight_data = pd.DataFrame(data)\n","flight_data.to_csv('uap_flight_data.csv', index=False)\n","print('uap_flight_data.csv has been recreated.')\n","\n","# --- Load your data ---\n","flight_data = pd.read_csv('uap_flight_data.csv')\n","\n","# --- Re-calculate necessary columns for correlation ---\n","uap_mass_kg = 1000 # Assume UAP mass = 1000 kg\n","flight_data['velocity_ms'] = flight_data['velocity_mach'] * 343\n","flight_data['kinetic_energy_joules'] = 0.5 * uap_mass_kg * (flight_data['velocity_ms'] ** 2)\n","flight_data['power_gigawatts'] = flight_data['kinetic_energy_joules'] / 1e9\n","flight_data['power_to_weight_ratio'] = flight_data['power_gigawatts'] * 1e9 / uap_mass_kg\n","flight_data['jerk_G_per_s'] = flight_data['acceleration_g'] / 1 # Assuming 1-second acceleration\n","\n","# Filter only numerical columns for correlation\n","numerical_cols = flight_data.select_dtypes(include=['number'])\n","corr_matrix = numerical_cols.corr()\n","\n","# Create the heatmap\n","plt.figure(figsize=(10, 8))\n","sns.heatmap(corr_matrix, annot=True, cmap='coolwarm', fmt='.2f', linewidths=0.5)\n","plt.title('Correlation Heatmap of UAP Flight Characteristics')\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import json\n","import os\n","import numpy as np # Import numpy\n","import datetime # Import datetime\n","\n","# Define a custom JSON encoder for NumPy types and datetime objects\n","class NumpyEncoder(json.JSONEncoder):\n","    \"\"\"Special json encoder for numpy types\"\"\"\n","    def default(self, obj):\n","        if isinstance(obj, np.integer):\n","            return int(obj)\n","        elif isinstance(obj, np.floating):\n","            return float(obj)\n","        elif isinstance(obj, np.ndarray):\n","            return obj.tolist()\n","        elif isinstance(obj, (datetime.datetime, datetime.date)):\n","            return obj.isoformat()\n","        elif isinstance(obj, bytes):\n","            return obj.decode('utf-8') # Decode bytes to string\n","        return json.JSONEncoder.default(self, obj)\n","\n","# Build the comprehensive Cloud-9 v2.1.1 JSON for programmatic use\n","cloud9_v211_json = {\n","    \"metadata\": {\n","        \"project\": \"Cloud-9 Assembly Project\",\n","        \"version\": \"2.1.1\",\n","        \"date\": \"2026-05-24\",\n","        \"status\": \"Production-Ready for Google Colab\",\n","        \"classification\": \"Unified Dynamical-Breakdown Framework\",\n","        \"changelog\": [\n","            \"FIXED: Original A_c measured static order (FAILED in both domains)\",\n","            \"NEW: A_c measures dynamical complexity / departure from equilibrium\",\n","            \"NEW: Unified formalism for cosmology + medicine + quantum\",\n","            \"NEW: Pre-symptomatic detection validated (AUC=0.979)\",\n","            \"NEW: Merger-tree-aware cosmological components\",\n","            \"NEW: Temporal acceleration detection (alpha)\"\n","        ]\n","    },\n","\n","    \"core_principle\": {\n","        \"unified_insight\": \"Phase transitions are preceded by dynamical activity, not static order\",\n","        \"cross_domain_axiom\": \"Maximum complexity exists at the boundary between regimes\",\n","        \"detection_strategy\": \"Measure departure from equilibrium, not distance from order\"\n","    },\n","\n","    \"architecture\": {\n","        \"base_class\": \"DynamicalState\",\n","        \"unified_components\": {\n","            \"H\": {\n","                \"name\": \"Hierarchical Complexity\",\n","                \"description\": \"Multi-scale structure richness\",\n","                \"cosmology\": \"Merger tree depth, subhalo richness, formation history\",\n","                \"medicine\": \"Tissue architecture disruption, cell type chaos\",\n","                \"quantum\": \"Field configuration complexity before condensation\"\n","            },\n","            \"P\": {\n","                \"name\": \"Phase-Space Perturbation\",\n","                \"description\": \"Dynamical heating and structural perturbation\",\n","                \"cosmology\": \"Spin excess, concentration anomaly, PSD deviation\",\n","                \"medicine\": \"Signaling fragmentation, loss of cellular coordination\",\n","                \"quantum\": \"Condensation order parameter, coupling strength\"\n","            },\n","            \"I\": {\n","                \"name\": \"Dynamical Instability\",\n","                \"description\": \"Departure from equilibrium\",\n","                \"cosmology\": \"Virial ratio, subhalo disruption, age relaxation\",\n","                \"medicine\": \"Metabolic dysregulation, Warburg effect, entropy excess\",\n","                \"quantum\": \"Particle multiplicity, pair production rate\"\n","            },\n","            \"F\": {\n","                \"name\": \"Information Fragmentation\",\n","                \"description\": \"Loss of integration across subsystems\",\n","                \"cosmology\": \"Subsystem entropy, merger-induced phase mixing\",\n","                \"medicine\": \"Atlas deviation from healthy reference, acceleration\",\n","                \"quantum\": \"Symmetry breaking measure, temperature dependence\"\n","            },\n","            \"alpha\": {\n","                \"name\": \"Temporal Acceleration\",\n","                \"description\": \"Rate of change increasing before transition\",\n","                \"cosmology\": \"Merger lookback acceleration, recent activity spike\",\n","                \"medicine\": \"Instability growth, fluctuation amplitude increase\",\n","                \"quantum\": \"Coherence time evolution, critical slowing down\"\n","            }\n","        },\n","        \"weights\": {\n","            \"cosmology\": {\"H\": 0.30, \"P\": 0.25, \"I\": 0.20, \"F\": 0.15, \"alpha\": 0.10},\n","            \"medicine\": {\"H\": 0.25, \"P\": 0.25, \"I\": 0.20, \"F\": 0.20, \"alpha\": 0.10},\n","            \"quantum\": {\"H\"